{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents.c1_exponent_vieta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents.c1_exponent_vieta","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1ModuleExponents.lean#L56-L67","doc":"**Vieta for the exponents.** If the exponent polynomial factors over `R` as\n`(t − λ₊)(t − λ₋)`, the exponents sum to `1 − q` (= `tr A(0)`) and multiply to `q − 1`\n(= `det A(0)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents.c1_root_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents.c1_root_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1ModuleExponents.lean#L50-L54","doc":"**Root reduction.** Every exponent `t` satisfies `t² = (1−q)t − (q−1)` — the order-2\nrelation the C1 recurrence imposes on its local solutions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents.c1_exponent_discriminant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents.c1_exponent_discriminant","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1ModuleExponents.lean#L44-L48","doc":"**Exponent discriminant** `(q−1)² − 4(q−1) = (q−1)(q−5)` — the exponent difference\n`(λ₊−λ₋)²`. Nonzero off `q ∈ {1,5}`, so the two local exponents at 0 are generically\ndistinct (diagonalisable local monodromy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents.c1ExponentPoly_eq_char","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents.c1ExponentPoly_eq_char","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1ModuleExponents.lean#L38-L42","doc":"**Char-polynomial form** `t² − (tr A(0))·t + det A(0)` with `tr A(0)=1−q`, `det A(0)=q−1`\n(witness-computed). Confirms `c1ExponentPoly` is the companion's characteristic polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents.c1ExponentPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1ModuleExponents.c1ExponentPoly","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1ModuleExponents.lean#L34-L36","doc":"**The C1 exponent polynomial at 0** `t² + (q−1)t + (q−1)` — the characteristic\npolynomial of the companion `A(0) = [[0,1],[1−q,1−q]]`. Its roots are the local exponents. ","signatureChunk":0}]}